# What's the weather?
# Type a city and Plain looks up the temperature there right now.
# Try: Show how many people live there too, with place's population.
# Try: Add &temperature_unit=fahrenheit to the end of the forecast address, and change °C to °F.
show "Type a city to see its weather. Press Enter on its own to stop."
repeat forever
    ask "Which city?" and call it city
    if city is empty
        stop repeating
    try
        read "https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search?name={city}&count=1" and call it places
        if places contains "results"
            set place to the first item of places's results
            read "https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?latitude={place's latitude}&longitude={place's longitude}&current=temperature_2m" and call it forecast
            show "It's {forecast's current's temperature 2m}°C in {place's name}, {place's country}."
        otherwise
            show "Plain couldn't find a place called {city}."
    if that fails
        show "Sorry, Plain couldn't get the weather for {city}."
        show the problem
show "Goodbye!"
